Create a reusable Skill named "add-cute-black-cat".

Description:
Simple one-command tool that takes one image path and uses Grok Imagine to add a cute anime-style black cat into the photo.

Usage (exactly as user wants):
/add-cute-black-cat <image_path>

Example:
/add-cute-black-cat photo.jpg
/add-cute-black-cat pic/my_dog.jpg

Automatic workflow:
1. Load the input image (first and only argument)
2. Use Grok Imagine's built-in image editing capability to add ONE cute anime black cat
3. Cat style: chibi / kawaii anime style, big sparkling eyes, small body, playful pose, glossy black fur with white accents
4. Cat placement: naturally integrated (on lap, on shoulder, sitting on table, peeking from corner, etc.) — make it look like it belongs in the scene
5. Preserve original photo lighting, style and quality as much as possible
6. Save output as "<original_filename>_with_cat.jpg" in the current folder
7. Print short log (including where the cat was placed)

Requirements:
- Store everything in .grok/skills/add-cute-black-cat/
- Include clear SKILL.md with usage examples
- Prefer using Grok Build's built-in Imagine / image-edit tool (do NOT write heavy Python code if possible)
- If a small Python wrapper is needed, keep it minimal and only for file handling
- Support any image format (jpg, png, etc.)
- Container-aware (Podman ubuntu) with --break-system-packages if needed

Generate the complete skill now.
